# Release-export hygiene.
#
# Exclude maintainer working-state from `git archive` exports / release
# tarballs so the distributed artefact is fork-clean. The public `.working/` tree
# HELD per-run QA records, session handoffs, metrics, decisions, and the
# detailed-CHANGELOG mirror (the maintainer's audit trail); that content moved to the
# private sibling in PR2b-3 (see the scope note below), and an adopter needs none of it.
#
# Scope note: `export-ignore` affects `git archive` only. The public `.working/`
# tree was removed from this repository in PR2b-3 (its canonical copy lives in the
# private sibling grc_library_private/.working/), so this block is retained as
# defence in depth: should any writer recreate a public `.working/`, it stays out
# of release tarballs. The removed tree remains in this repository's git history;
# true history cleanliness is a separate history-rewrite step.
.working/ export-ignore
